<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fuzhou</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Foochow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fuzhou is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> province in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the Min river near the coast. As Dongye it was the capital of the Minyue kingdom in the 2nd century BCE, and in the 10th century it was the seat of the Min kingdom. Opened to foreign trade as a treaty port in 1842, it became a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> trade and the site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou-navy-yard">Fuzhou Navy Yard</a>, founded in 1866.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fuzhou.jpg" alt="Fuzhou" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Listwiseafford · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fuzhou_Taixi_CBD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
